      "claim": "The concept of 'fair trade' fundamentally requires voluntary participation and equitable terms between independent economic agents with the ability to exit the relationship.",
      "evidence": "Standard economic and ethical definitions of fair trade emphasize the absence of coercion, exploitation, and significant power imbalances that prevent free negotiation.",
